# Build artifacts
/target

# Cargo.lock is checked in for reproducible builds of the compliance
# binary crate. For library crates the convention is to gitignore it,
# but this workspace contains a binary-like member (compliance handlers)
# whose exact dependency resolution matters for conformance runs.
# Decision: CHECK IN Cargo.lock (do not ignore it).
# Ref: https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/faq.html#why-have-cargolock-in-version-control

